"when built into a shared library: it is mutable, with external linkage "
"and`&nbsp;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28285
msgid ""
"Warns when objects which are supposed to be globally unique might get "
"duplicated when built into a shared library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28288
msgid ""
"This can occur to objects which are hidden from the dynamic linker, due to "
"having hidden visibility (on posix) or lacking a dllimport/dllexport "
"attribute (on windows). If such an object is built into a shared library, "
"each instance of the library will get its own copy. This can cause very "
"subtle bugs if there was only supposed to be one copy of the object in "
"question: singletons aren't single, changes to one object won't affect the "
"others, the object's initializer will run once per copy, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28296
msgid "Specifically, this warning fires when it detects an object which:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28298
msgid ""
"Is defined as `inline` in a header file (so it might get compiled into "
"multiple libaries), and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28299
msgid "Has external linkage (otherwise it's supposed to be duplicated), and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28300
msgid ""
"Has hidden visibility (posix) or lacks a dllimport/dllexport attribute "
"(windows)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28302
msgid "As well as one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28304
msgid "The object is mutable, or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28305
msgid "The object's initializer definitely has side effects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28307
msgid ""
"The warning can be resolved by removing one of the conditions above. In "
"rough order of preference, this may be done by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28310
msgid "Marking the object `const` (if possible)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28311
msgid "Moving the object's definition to a source file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28312
msgid ""
"Making the object visible using `__attribute((visibility(\"default\")))`, "
"`__declspec(dllimport)`, or `__declspec(dllexport)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28315
msgid ""
"When annotating an object with `__declspec(dllimport)` or "
"`__declspec(dllexport)`, take care to ensure that the object is only "
"exported from one dll, and is imported everywhere else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DiagnosticsReference.md:28319
msgid ""
"Note that for (2), all levels of a pointer variable must be constant; `const "
"int*` will trigger the warning because the pointer itself is mutable."
msgstr ""

